{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_010: scgpt+resnet50+avgpool+weighted, acc=0.525), the evidence is sparse and the most critical uncertainty is whether the image encoder is a bottleneck. Config_020 makes a single clean change—upgrading resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l—while holding all other factors (scgpt, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal) constant. This isolates the contribution of a stronger pretrained image encoder, which is likely a major driver of multimodal performance. If ViT-L improves accuracy, it justifies investing remaining budget in ViT-L-based configs; if not, we save substantial GPU hours by sticking with ResNet50. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high, roughly 6–7 GPU hours (ViT-L has ~300M params vs ResNet50's ~25M, increasing per-step compute), but this is a pivotal architectural decision worth the investment given 8 experiments remain."
}

